      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 4 at 3:32PM HST until November 6 at 6:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY WILL BE IN EFFECT FOR THE NORTH AND WEST\nFACING SHORES OF NIIHAU KAUAI OAHU AND MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING\nSHORES OF MAUI FROM THURSDAY MORNING THROUGH EARLY FRIDAY\nMORNING...\n\n..A moderate size, long period north northwest swell will arrive\nearly Thursday and fill in around the island chain through the\nmorning. This swell will lift surf heights to advisory level\nthresholds along north-facing and west-facing shores.\n\n* WHAT...Surf heights of between 14 to 18 feet along north-facing\nshores, 10 to 14 feet along west-facing shores.\n\n* WHERE...The north-facing and west-facing shores of Niihau,\nKauai, Oahu and Molokai and the north-facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM Thursday to 6 AM HST Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
