  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 050502\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 PM HST Wed Nov 04 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with a broad area of low\npressure located over the eastern portion of the Central Pacific\nbasin are showing some signs of organization.  Environmental\nconditions appear conducive for additional development of this\nsystem, and a tropical depression is likely to form over the\nCentral Pacific basin during the next few days while it moves\nwestward to west-northwestward at 10 to 15 mph.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...medium...60 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...70 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Blake\nNNNN",
